# Offizier lead (M6, D-096, lead = true): the flag bearer of the file. The
# same officer as `offizier` (same hitbox, anims and poses), plus a thin
# k-outlined staff l with a Y/o finial in a k cap and a small flag (k
# outline): the Kaiserfahne, a Y/o field with a dark d eagle blot. Above
# row 10 the staff uses only columns 0-2, so it ends >= 2 px left of the
# 8 px sabre zone (columns 4-11).
# march: flag up behind the shako, the cloth flutters. habtacht: the flag
# dips (the staff slants up-left to the sprite edge, the cloth hangs limp
# as a 2 px strip under it); the sabre is half drawn as for `offizier`.
# praesentiert: the staff stands up tall, finial at row 2, cloth spread;
# the sabre is drawn as for `offizier`.
# squished: the flag lies on the ground behind him.
# Faces right; mirror = auto. Built with the same scratch script (plus a
# pixel post-pass for the art-director's round 1 fixes).
sprite = offizier_lead
size   = 16x32
origin = 8,32
hitbox = 2,10,12,22
mirror = auto
anim   = march        frames=2 ticks=8 loop
anim   = habtacht     frames=1
anim   = praesentiert frames=1
anim   = squished     frames=1
